# Production release signing configuration template.
#
# Copy this file to a name that is git-ignored, for example:
#   release.properties            (ignored only if added to .gitignore)
#   ~/.config/kaminarinfty/release.properties   (outside the repository)
#
# Then fill in the real values. Do not commit real passwords or keystore paths.
#
# The release signing config in app/build.gradle.kts reads from:
#   1. Environment variables - highest priority
#      KEYSTORE_PATH, STORE_PASSWORD, KEY_PASSWORD
#   2. Gradle project properties - read from -P flags or from this file when
#      loaded explicitly by the owner before building.
#      releaseKeystorePath, releaseStorePassword, releaseKeyPassword
#
# Required values:
releaseKeystorePath=/absolute/path/to/my-upload-key.jks
releaseStorePassword=REPLACE_WITH_ACTUAL_STORE_PASSWORD
releaseKeyPassword=REPLACE_WITH_ACTUAL_KEY_PASSWORD

# Optional owner notes:
# - Keep the keystore and this file separate from the repository.
# - Back up the keystore and these passwords securely and separately.
# - Losing the production key means losing the ability to publish updates to the
#   same app identity on the Play Store / installed devices.
